exports[`model-derived exports keep pace with the model > renders the whole construct set the same way run to run 1`] = `
"# Completeness API

> Version 9.0.0 — OpenAPI 3.1.0

Base URL: https://api.example.test/v9

More: https://docs.example.test — Handbook

Every construct a normalized operation can carry, in one document.

## Servers

- https://api.example.test/v9 — Production

## Authentication

- \`apiKeyAuth\` (apiKey, header \`X-Api-Key\`)

Applies to every operation unless overridden — one of:

- \`apiKeyAuth\`

---

# Create a thing

\`\`\`http
POST https://api.example.test/v9/things/{thingId}
\`\`\`

> Deprecated

- Operation ID: \`createThing\`
- Tags: Things
- More: https://docs.example.test/things

Creates a thing and schedules its indexing.

## Servers

These override the base URL above for this operation:

- https://ops.example.test/v9 — Ops plane

## Authentication

One of the following (each line = every scheme in it):

- \`apiKeyAuth\` (scopes: things:write)

## Path parameters

- \`thingId\` (string, required) — Identifier of the thing.

## Request body — \`application/json\` (required)

- \`label\` (string, required)

## Responses

### 201 — Created.

Body \`application/json\`:

- \`id\` (string)

## Callbacks

### indexed — POST {$request.body#/callbackUrl}

Sent once the thing is indexed.

Payload \`application/json\`:

- \`id\` (string)

Expected responses from your server:

- 204 — Acknowledged.

---

# Webhook: Thing changed

> Event "thingChanged" sent by the API to your webhook endpoint via POST.

## Request body — \`application/json\`

- \`id\` (string)

## Responses

### 204 — Acknowledged.
"
